[00:00.85]Lesson 27 | 第27课
[00:03.95]The 'Vasa' | “瓦萨”号
[00:12.34]What happened to the 'Vasa' almost immediately after she was launched? | “瓦萨”号下水后几乎立即发生了什么？
[00:20.57]From the seventeenth-century empire of Sweden, | 在17世纪的瑞典帝国，
[00:24.32]the story of a galleon that sank at the start of her maiden voyage in 1628 must be one of the strangest tales of the sea. | 一艘大型帆船在1628年首次航行刚开始时便沉没，这个故事一定是航海史上最离奇的事件之一。
[00:34.84]For nearly three and a half centuries she lay at the bottom of Stockholm harbour until her discovery in 1956. | 在被发现之前，“瓦萨”号在斯德哥尔摩港的海底沉睡了将近三个半世纪，直到1956年才重见天日。
[00:44.34]This was the Vasa, royal flagship of the great imperial fleet. | 这就是“瓦萨”号，强大瑞典帝国舰队的皇家旗舰。
[00:51.53]King Gustavus Adolphus 'The Northern Hurricane', | 国王古斯塔夫·阿道夫，人称“北方飓风”，
[00:56.23]then at the height of his military success in the 'Thirty Years' War, | 当时正处于“三十年战争”中军事成就的巅峰时期，
[01:01.33]had dictated her measurements and armament. | 亲自规定了这艘船的尺寸和武器装备。
[01:05.42]Triple gun-decks mounted sixty-four bronze cannon. | 三层炮甲板上装有64门青铜大炮。
[01:10.73]She was intended to play a leading role in the growing might of Sweden. | 这艘船原本被寄望于在瑞典日益增强的国力中发挥重要作用。
[01:16.84]As she was prepared for her maiden voyage on August 10, 1628, Stockholm was in a ferment. | 1628年8月10日，“瓦萨”号准备首次航行，整个斯德哥尔摩都沸腾了。
[01:27.58]From the Skeppsbron and surrounding islands | 人们从斯凯普斯布隆一带及周围岛屿上，
[01:30.64]the people watched this thing of beauty begin to spread her sails and catch the wind. | 注视着这艘美丽的船扬起风帆，迎风启航。
[01:37.80]They had laboured for three years to produce this floating work of art; | 人们辛苦劳作了三年，才建造出这件漂浮在水上的艺术品；
[01:44.16]she was more richly carved and ornamented than any previous ship. | 它的雕刻和装饰比以往任何一艘船都更加精美华丽。
[01:50.09]The high stern castle was a riot of carved gods, demons, knights, kings, warriors, | 高耸的船尾楼上布满了雕刻，题材包括众神、恶魔、骑士、国王和武士，
[01:58.90]mermaids, cherubs; and zoomorphic animal shapes ablaze with red and gold and blue, | 还有美人鱼、小天使以及各种动物造型的雕饰，红、金、蓝三色交相辉映，
[02:06.37]symbols of courage, power, and cruelty, | 这些雕饰象征着勇气、力量和残酷，
[02:10.57]were portrayed to stir the imaginations of the superstitious sailors of the day. | 它们旨在激发当时那些迷信水手的想象力。
[02:17.23]Then the cannons of the anchored warships thundered a salute to which the Vasa fired in reply. | 随后，停泊在港内的军舰鸣炮致敬，“瓦萨”号也鸣炮回应。
[02:25.64]As she emerged from her drifting cloud of gun smoke with the water churned to foam beneath her bow, | 当它从弥漫的硝烟中驶出，船头下的海水翻腾起泡沫，
[02:32.92]her flags flying, pennants waving, sails filling in the breeze, | 旗帜飘扬，三角旗招展，风帆迎风鼓起，
[02:39.53]and the red and gold of her superstructure ablaze with colour, | 上层建筑的红色与金色也绚丽夺目，
[02:44.92]she presented a more majestic spectacle than Stockholmers had ever seen before. | 它呈现出斯德哥尔摩人前所未见的雄伟景象。
[02:51.50]All gun-ports were open and the muzzles peeped wickedly from them. | 所有炮门都敞开着，炮口从里面探出，显得杀气腾腾。
[02:58.11]As the wind freshened there came a sudden squall and the ship made a strange movement, listing to port. | 随着风势增强，一阵突如其来的飑风袭来，船身突然出现异常，向左舷倾斜。
[03:06.16]The Ordnance officer ordered all the port cannon to be heaved to starboard | 军械军官下令将左舷所有大炮移向右舷，
[03:11.68]to counteract the list but the steepening angle of the decks increased. | 以抵消船身的倾斜，但甲板的倾斜程度反而进一步加剧。
[03:18.28]Then the sound of rumbling thunder reached the watchers on the shore, | 接着，隆隆的雷鸣般声响传到了岸上观望者的耳中，
[03:22.91]as cargo, ballast, ammunition and 400 people went sliding and crashing down to the port side of the steeply listing ship. | 原来，货物、压舱物、弹药和400人都滑向急剧倾斜的船只左舷，发出一片碰撞声。
[03:33.99]The lower gun-ports were now below water and the inrush sealed the ship's fate. | 此时，下层炮门已经没入水中，涌入的海水就此决定了这艘船的命运。
[03:41.03]In that first glorious hour, the mighty Vasa, which was intended to rule the Baltic, | 就在它首航的最初时刻，这艘原本被寄望于称霸波罗的海的强大“瓦萨”号，
[03:48.67]sank with all flags flying—in the harbour of her birth. | 在旗帜依然飘扬之际，沉没在它诞生的港湾中。